I haven’t incorporated media queries in the CSS for this landing page, which means it won’t be fully responsive or display properly on smaller devices like phones or tablets.
The design and layout are primarily meant for larger screens.
This project is intended just to showcase the skills and concepts I’ve learned so far, rather than a polished, fully responsive website.


🧋 BobaTea Landing Page

A modern, responsive landing page for a fictional bubble tea brand. Designed to be visually appealing with smooth animations, playful colors, and a slideshow to showcase products.


---

🚀 Features

Full-screen design with split background gradient

Navigation bar with animated hover effects

Brand logo + name displayed prominently

Image Slideshow that automatically changes every 3 seconds

Catchy taglines and brand description text

Interactive Buttons with smooth text-slide animation on hover

Fun fact section about bubble tea

Social Media Icons with hover lift animation

Responsive Layout for different screen sizes



---

🛠 Tech Stack

HTML5 – Page structure

CSS3 – Layout, animations, gradients, and hover effects

JavaScript (Vanilla) – Automatic image slideshow functionality

Font Awesome – Social media icons

Google Fonts (Poppins) – Clean, modern typography




